{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc 'rtk read /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/behavior.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/architecture.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/references/glossary.md /Users/yousefallaban/.codex/plugins/cache/yousefallaban/scrubjay/0.1.0/skills/docs-conventions/assets/behavior-capability.md'","aggregated_output":"Purpose: rules for `behavior/<domain>/<capability>.md`. Template: `assets/behavior-capability.md`.\n\nFrontmatter: `capability`, as `<domain>/<capability>`.\n\nTitle: the capability as a verb phrase, such as \"Save an item to the wishlist\".\n\nBody: the claims, in the claim format, 3 to 7 of them, and nothing else. Observable behavior only. Owners live in index.md, history in git, code locations in architecture/boundaries.md, and how it's built in architecture/.\n\nWritten by docs-map when a domain is mapped and by spec-ship when a spec ships, which copies the spec's claims without rewording and applies each Add, Change and Remove. Never edited by hand during a spec; a change to a claim is a Change in the spec that ships it.\nPurpose: rules for `architecture/<area>.md`. Templates: `assets/architecture/<area>.md`.\n\nFrontmatter: `area`, the area name. A title, then the area's own table or list. Current state only: no history, no plans. The why links to decision records.\n\nArea files are created the first time they have content, never empty. `stack.md` exists from init, with the commands spec-build and spec-ship run. The folder listing is its own index.\n\n| Area | Holds |\n| --- | --- |\n| `stack` | languages and frameworks, and the commands to install, run, test, lint and build |\n| `conventions` | only the rules agents get wrong without being told: naming, error handling, test style |\n| `boundaries` | modules: name, path, domain, what each may depend on |\n| `data-model` | entities: name, key fields, relations |\n| `contracts` | APIs and events: name, kind, input, output, consumers |\n| `integrations` | external services: purpose, direction, auth, what the product does when it fails |\n| `config` | settings and flags: name, purpose, default, where it's set; never real secret values |\n| `invariants` | non-negotiable rules every spec must keep: ID, rule, why |\n\nWritten by docs-map for what a domain needs, and by spec-ship for the files plan.md lists under Architecture to update at ship.\nPurpose: rules for `glossary.md`. No template.\n\nOne line per term, sorted A to Z, created when the first term settles:\n`- **Term**: meaning in product language. Code: \\`Name\\`. Avoid: other words.`\n`Code` and `Avoid` are optional.\n\nA term is written the moment it settles, during grilling or docs-map. Business rules never go in the glossary; a rule found while writing a term becomes a claim in behavior/.\n---\ncapability: \"{{domain}}/{{capability}}\"\n---\n# {{Capability as a verb phrase}}\n\n- {{Actor}} {{does or sees something observable, present tense}} {#{{claim-id}}}\n  e.g. {{a concrete situation}} -> {{the observable result}}\n\n<!-- 3 to 7 claims, observable behavior only (\"keeps one entry\", never \"uses a unique index\").\nNothing else goes in this file: owners live in index.md, history in git,\ncode locations in architecture/boundaries.md. -->\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
